| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | test/integration/pty_harness.dart | 💡 suggestion release harness resources on the loud failure path too try finally close s doc contract cancel the output subscription otherwise an open stream keeps the test runner s event loop alive and delete the harness owned temp cwd after the process is dead the new body runs shutdownpty before those calls — so when escalation fails and shutdownpty throws its loud stateerror the rest of close is skipped outputsub cancel releaseownedcwd and releasetranscript never run the old semantics always released silent give up the new semantics trade resource release for loudness but you can have both dart future void close async if closed return closed true try await shutdownpty pty budgetscale waitbudgetscale finally await outputsub cancel releaseownedcwd releasetranscript the stateerror still propagates and fails the test loudly the subscription is detached and the temp cwd is cleaned up on dev machines where the process does not exit immediately after same shape applies to hardkill line 528 whose body likewise puts shutdownpty first |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

